  "scope": "Complete product root-start coordination moves to the adapter while the same native owner keeps live admission, identity reservations, group startup and atomic commit-before-publication. The frozen pre-migration root independently compares coordinator order and native state; SQLite fault injection compares journal tables, consumed identities and restart behavior.",
  "limitations": [
    "This remains a Leserpent product adapter, not the generic standalone runtime core. Callers must bound ingress, enforce quotas and supply a real principal/capability snapshot and remaining budget. Static authorization is not a live grant.",
    "Host hooks are trusted, stateful and once-only. Earlier successful reservations are not refunded on later refusal or unwind; native side effects are not rolled back by the adapter. Native journal admission must be rechecked before commit.",
    "The root oracle retains the whole previous entry and shares previously verified HIR authorization, computation, request construction and group implementation. It proves coordinator parity, not independent implementations of every lower-level validator.",
    "Timed clock validation and due-work expiration remain in the native wrapper. Restore/reply admission, native journals, full host-neutral durable recovery, complete vertical compatibility and physical extraction remain open. No native maturity promotion is claimed.",
    "Local macOS Rust/SQLite verification only; no new Linux, GUI or remote CI execution.",
    "The previous standalone checkpoint was reused after rechecking 270 copied sources and 280 exported files. No new standalone export or standalone test run was performed."
  ],
